{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1773948764,"nonce":"BlNcJF8ZFEIbl1FL9dt/LWEaUpM=","title":"Umbrella: user-configurable policies and behavior in Mandible","message":"The user has repeatedly expressed a desire to make Mandible behavior configurable rather than hardcoded. This umbrella tracks all the places where policy decisions are currently hardcoded and should eventually be exposed as user settings.\n\nKnown instances (as of 2026-03-19):\n- Inbox ack scoping: auth_results are globally ackable; should be scopeable to originating agent (b47891b)\n- Auth request TTL: hardcoded 24h (auth-queue.ts:15)\n- Resolved item visibility window: hardcoded 1h (auth-queue.ts:16)\n- Stuck approval recovery threshold: hardcoded 10min (auth-queue.ts:718)\n- Inbox issue visibility: which agents see which issues (currently all open issues shown to all agents)\n- Protected branch fallback order: hardcoded develop→main\n- Content-dependent transform timeouts: hardcoded thresholds\n\nDesign direction (from 2026-03-19 conversation):\n- Settings should live in Mandible settings DB, exposed via settings UI\n- Some policies may be per-repo, others global\n- The inbox redesign (inbox_items table, work-queue dispatch model) is a prerequisite for several of these\n\nSee also: issue 350817b (dirty-worktree policy inconsistency)","files":null}]}